"Created `migration/cutover_rollback.md` with three sections:\n\n**Cutover Steps** (8 steps): verify replication health → final shadow comparison → freeze writes (`freeze.sh`) → final sync → switch traffic → resume dual read/write → validate against `new_state.json` → record new baseline.\n\n**Rollback Plan** (6 steps) with explicit triggers (cutover failure, unexpected shadow-compare diffs, validation failures): freeze the new system → repoint traffic to the old state → restore/reconcile from the `baseline.json` snapshot → remove the frozen flag → verify via `dual_rw.log` → document the incident.\n\n**Residue Check** — the command to list files modified in the last 10 minutes:\n\n```bash\nfind . -type f -mmin -10 -print\n```\n\nI verified the command works — running it in the migration directory listed all 28 recently touched files, including the migration artifacts (`baseline.json`, `dual_rw.log`, `frozen.flag`, etc.) and the `.git` internals from the initial `git init`. The doc notes to review the output for stray leftovers like `frozen.flag` before declaring the procedure complete."